A(('p', '13.2 Neighboring parables. The Talents, the Minas, the Ten Virgins, and the Thief and the Watchful Servants are each read in their own study of the Parable Studies. This story makes no use of their meanings, and they make none of this one.'))
A(('p', '13.3 Final Synthesis. Jesus asks who is a faithful and wise servant whom his lord has made ruler over his household to give them meat in due season. That servant is blessed when his lord comes and finds him so doing, and is made ruler over all his goods. Another servant says in his heart that his lord delays and abuses those under him, and his lord comes in a day and hour he does not expect and cuts him asunder. Luke adds the servant who knew his lord’s will and the statement that much is required of those given much. Jesus names no part of the story.'))
